    "abstract": "Hyper Text Markup Language (HTML) is the main markup language for creating web\npages and other information that can be displayed in a web browser. HTML5 is the fifth\nrevision of the HTML standard. Its aim is to deliver almost everything you want to do without\nrequiring additional plug-in. HTML5 first describes new tags for multimedia, which are the\nnew audio and video tags. We produced an implementation of HTTP Live Streaming (HLS)\nfor an IP camera by using elements of HTML5 for media playback. This implementation\nfollows HLS standard in which we utilizes an open source library named FFMPEG. A\nconclusion of this paper is that live steaming on mobile devices over HTTP is achieved\nwithout any plug-ins.",
